{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Written in this book of the Torah.</b> And above it says ״גַּם כָּל חֳלִי וְכָל מַכָּה … בְּסֵפֶר הַתּוֹרָה הַזֹּאת״? הַזֹּאת — feminine form, referring to הַתּוֹרָה; הַזֶּה — masculine form, referring to הַסֵּפֶר. And by means of the cantillation parsing they are divided into two forms: in the section of the curses, the tipcha is placed under בְּסֵפֶר, and הַתּוֹרָה הַזֹּאת are joined together — therefore it says הַזֹּאת. But here the tipcha is placed under הַתּוֹרָה, so that סֵפֶר הַתּוֹרָה are joined together — therefore the masculine form follows it, for the word refers to הַסֵּפֶר."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:55.795858717Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}